<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Autocracy</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as autocratic</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Autocracy is a system of government in which supreme power is held by a single ruler, unconstrained by legal or institutional limits. The Russian tsars explicitly claimed autocratic power, and resistance to reform contributed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>'s fall. Elements of autocratic rule are also discussed for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire</a>.</p></div>
